  "narrative": "All new estimates are signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 dependency outcomes, a positive signed estimate means stronger dependency, more negative score, in the exposed or subgroup comparison. For direction +1 NFE2L2 outcomes, a positive signed estimate means weaker, less negative NFE2L2 dependency, the observed reversal of the original synthetic-lethality expectation. I benchmarked clinical relevance using roughly 10 percent of the absolute outcome mean, with approximate thresholds SMARCA2 0.0415, WRN 0.0301, NFE2L2 0.0093, RPL11 0.0252, KIF18A 0.0256, and TMED10 0.0253. The accepted SMARCA2 association is highly specific rather than generic ARID1A or library context. In ARID1A-negative models, SMARCA4 loss retains a huge signed SMARCA2 effect R32 +0.776 CI +0.754 to +0.798, supporting H34. In non-Avana library screens, the SMARCA4 effect remains large R28 +0.793 CI +0.735 to +0.850, supporting H30. By contrast, ARID1A loss alone among SMARCA4-loss-negative models is not clinically meaningful R27 +0.0023 CI -0.0211 to +0.0257; the upper bound is below the SMARCA2 relevance threshold, so H29 is rejected and closed. This refines H6 to a SMARCA4-loss-specific association in this dataset, not an ARID1A-only association. H22 remains possible but nondefinitive and is deferred rather than pursued immediately because its interaction interval is wide and the main SMARCA2 signal is already well supported. The accepted NFE2L2 reversal is robust across several same-dataset contexts. Outside Avana screens R29 +0.794 CI +0.744 to +0.844 supports H31; in STK11-loss co-occurring models R30 +0.773 CI +0.719 to +0.828 supports H32; in higher hypoxia R35 +0.781 CI +0.750 to +0.813 supports H37. These estimates are far above the small NFE2L2 relevance threshold and support the reversed H17 direction associatively. The accepted WRN association is also stable in pre-specified strata: high mutation burden R31 +0.781 CI +0.749 to +0.812 supports H33, and higher proliferation R34 +0.776 CI +0.733 to +0.820 supports H36. H33 should be interpreted cautiously as a near-tautological stratification because MSI-high models appear essentially all high-TMB, as indicated by the invalid H25 interaction with an empty exposed complement. Thus it is not independent biological validation, but it does show that the WRN association persists when the comparator is restricted to high-TMB models. H35 is the only near-threshold technical interaction: Cas9 activity greater or equal to 0.846 has a positive interaction estimate R33 +0.0519 CI -0.0010 to +0.1047. This is close to the SMARCA2 clinical threshold and the lower bound is nearly null, so a modest attenuation or modification in lower-Cas9 screens remains possible but not established. Given multiplicity, the small interaction magnitude, and its technical rather than biological priority, I keep H35 unresolved and deferred. The MYC and EGFR endpoint follow-ups are negative or nondefinitive. MYC amplification is not associated with clinically meaningful stronger RPL11 dependency R36 -0.0063 CI -0.0288 to +0.0162, so H38 is rejected and closed. For KIF18A R37 +0.0090 CI -0.0145 to +0.0324 and TMED10 R38 +0.0080 CI -0.0244 to +0.0403, point estimates are below relevance thresholds although upper intervals cross them; these are unresolved but deferred because they are weaker and lower priority than remaining untested outcomes and specificity controls. I am requesting independent validation for H17 rather than H35 because H17 is the accepted main association with a direction opposite to expectation and is therefore the most valuable large claim to confirm outside the discovery split. The new proposal set adds cross-exposure and negative-marker specificity checks, not as biological claims but as calibration for whether the very large accepted associations are outcome- and predictor-specific or reflect broader confounding. Overall, the evidence supports dataset-specific associations for SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, and KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; these remain associative within DNA-omics lung models and do not establish causality or generalizability.",
